{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The target omits anthropogenic heat release as a primary driver of the nocturnal UHI and instead identifies the urban sky view factor as the single governing mechanism. This conflicts with the problem's scope, which asks for a single mechanism that best explains why the night-time gap is larger in some cities than in others. The target's own counterconditions concede that anthropogenic heat or thermal mass may dominate the sky-view effect, which contradicts the claim that the UHI is 'governed by' sky view factor.","premise":"The problem asks for the single mechanism that best explains the cross-city variation in the nocturnal UHI, yet the target's counterconditions concede that anthropogenic heat or thermal mass can dominate sky view factor, undermining the claim that sky view factor is the single best explanatory mechanism.","premise_evidence":[{"block":"a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8","quote":"If thermal mass or anthropogenic heat dominates, sky view factor is not the single best explanatory mechanism."}],"target":"fea4fe44082b8189e3d76c876d4195c8018800e5ae362677f57a5e7924f575a7"}]}